-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled ELF FunctionID databases (ADR-043 Phase 2)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The worker container image bundles ELF FunctionID databases (.fidbf) generated
from the permissively-licensed libraries listed below (the authoritative, CI-gated
source set is deploy/fid/sources.toml). These databases contain ONLY non-reversible
function-body hashes, lifted symbol names, and library metadata — they contain NO
library code and NO source (the FLIRT "hashes + names, no code" rationale; see
docs/security/fid-database-licensing.md). They are shipped only from
permissively-licensed sources (Zlib / MIT / Apache-2.0 / BSL-1.0 / BSD-2-Clause /
BSD-3-Clause); copyleft sources (LGPL/GPL/AGPL, OpenSSL pre-3.0) are excluded and
gated out of the build.

  - zlib       (SPDX: Zlib)        https://zlib.net/
  - musl libc  (SPDX: MIT)         https://musl.libc.org/
  - OpenSSL    (SPDX: Apache-2.0)  https://www.openssl.org/   (3.0+ only)
  - Boost      (SPDX: BSL-1.0)     https://www.boost.org/

Per-database provenance manifests (source version + digest, compiler/flags, Ghidra
+ generator version, .fidbf digest, SPDX license) accompany each shipped database,
and per-source SPDX license ids are recorded in the per-release SBOM
(std-supplychain). Each source library's own copyright/attribution notice is
preserved as required by its license.
